\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Recursive refinement at one output position. The base step produces $z^{(0)}$. The same refinement operator $F$ maps $z^{(k)}$ to $z^{(k+1)}$ using the previous token embedding, the base attention context, and the soft embedding $p^{(k)}E$ of the current prediction. The shared output head emits a distribution at every depth; no new parameters are added as depth grows.}}{4}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:refine}{{2}{4}{Recursive refinement at one output position. The base step produces $z^{(0)}$. The same refinement operator $F$ maps $z^{(k)}$ to $z^{(k+1)}$ using the previous token embedding, the base attention context, and the soft embedding $p^{(k)}E$ of the current prediction. The shared output head emits a distribution at every depth; no new parameters are added as depth grows}{figure.caption.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Causal token-level halting. Each gate reads only signals computed before the refinement it controls, so a stopped token never consults the computation it skips. The predicted exit depth is not the same quantity as executed work: the active-subset executor runs a cell only on continuing rows, and forward hooks verify the intercepted call count against $N_{\mathrm  {cell}}$.}}{4}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:halt}{{3}{4}{Causal token-level halting. Each gate reads only signals computed before the refinement it controls, so a stopped token never consults the computation it skips. The predicted exit depth is not the same quantity as executed work: the active-subset executor runs a cell only on continuing rows, and forward hooks verify the intercepted call count against $N_{\mathrm {cell}}$}{figure.caption.3}{}}
